THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
======================

Fovea links one third-party dependency, resolved by Swift Package Manager
and declared in project.yml.

swift-markdown
  https://github.com/apple/swift-markdown
  Copyright (c) Apple Inc. and the Swift project authors
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, with the Swift runtime
  library exception. See <https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0>.

  Apache-2.0 is one-way compatible with GPLv3: the combined work is
  distributed under the GPLv3 terms, while swift-markdown itself remains
  under Apache-2.0.

  swift-markdown is used to obtain a CommonMark/GFM syntax tree carrying
  source ranges. The tree is never re-serialized — see
  docs/PRINCIPLES.md §3.1.

Everything else the app uses is part of macOS: AppKit, TextKit 2, SwiftUI
and the system fonts. Syntax highlighting is homegrown, deliberately, so
that no highlighting engine is bundled — see docs/PRINCIPLES.md §4.3.
